# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up your workflow code to write logs, report errors to your local notebook, and save partial work when a job is canceled. To read these outputs from your local notebook, see [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Configure le code de ton workflow pour écrire des logs, signaler des erreurs à ton notebook local et enregistrer le travail partiel lorsqu'un job est annulé. Pour lire ces sorties depuis ton notebook local, consulte [Exécuter un workflow géré](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| In the workflow | In your local notebook |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Write with a logger from the `logging` module, or call `print()`. | `job.logs()` returns the lines. |\n"
"| Raise an exception, or exit with a nonzero code. | `job.status()` returns `ERROR`, and `job.logs()` shows the traceback. |\n"
"| Call `send_error()`. | `job.error_message()` and `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` return the code, message, and details. |\n"
"| Call `save_result()` in a `SIGTERM` handler. | `job.result()` returns the partial result of a canceled job. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Dans le workflow | Dans ton notebook local |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Écris avec un logger du module `logging`, ou appelle `print()`. | `job.logs()` renvoie les lignes. |\n"
"| Lève une exception, ou quitte avec un code non nul. | `job.status()` renvoie `ERROR`, et `job.logs()` affiche la trace d'appels. |\n"
"| Appelle `send_error()`. | `job.error_message()` et `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` renvoient le code, le message et les détails. |\n"
"| Appelle `save_result()` dans un gestionnaire `SIGTERM`. | `job.result()` renvoie le résultat partiel d'un job annulé. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs {#write-logs}"
msgstr "Écrire des logs {#write-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. Read the logs with `job.logs()` while the job runs or after it ends.\n"
msgstr "Tout ce que le workflow écrit sur la sortie standard ou l'erreur standard va dans les logs du job. Lis les logs avec `job.logs()` pendant l'exécution du job ou après sa fin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up a logger {#set-up-a-logger}"
msgstr "Configurer un logger {#set-up-a-logger}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the `logging` module from the Python standard library. `logging.basicConfig()` writes to standard error, which reaches the logs without delay. The format in the following example adds a timestamp to each line:\n"
msgstr "Utilise le module `logging` de la bibliothèque standard Python. `logging.basicConfig()` écrit sur l'erreur standard, qui atteint les logs sans délai. Le format de l'exemple suivant ajoute un horodatage à chaque ligne :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`level=logging.WARNING` hides `INFO` messages from other packages, and `logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` keeps `INFO` messages for your own logger. `qiskit_ibm_runtime` sets its own level with the `QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL` environment variable.\n"
msgstr "`level=logging.WARNING` masque les messages `INFO` des autres paquets, et `logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` conserve les messages `INFO` pour ton propre logger. `qiskit_ibm_runtime` définit son propre niveau avec la variable d'environnement `QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`print()` also reaches the logs, but standard output is buffered, so printed lines might not appear until the job ends. If you use `print()`, pass `flush=True`.\n"
msgstr "`print()` atteint aussi les logs, mais la sortie standard est mise en tampon, donc les lignes affichées peuvent n'apparaître qu'à la fin du job. Si tu utilises `print()`, passe `flush=True`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: get_logger() from qiskit_serverless adds a [PUBLIC] prefix that Functions uses to split provider and user logs for Catalog Functions; custom workflow logs strip it. Tested with 0.37.0: its lines have no timestamp, and logger.exception() and exc_info=True drop the traceback (PrefixFormatter builds new records with exc_info=None). Confirm whether to recommend the standard logging module for custom workflows, or to fix get_logger(). */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the log level for each run {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"
msgstr "Définir le niveau de log pour chaque exécution {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To debug one run without changing the code, pass the log level as an argument:\n"
msgstr "Pour déboguer une exécution sans modifier le code, passe le niveau de log en argument :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, set the level of your logger from the argument:\n"
msgstr "Pour activer cela, définis le niveau de ton logger à partir de l'argument :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow has an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), declare `log_level` in it, for example as `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\"]}`.\n"
msgstr "Si le workflow a un [schéma d'arguments](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), déclare-y `log_level`, par exemple sous la forme `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\"]}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: decide what to log {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"
msgstr "Bonne pratique : décider quoi journaliser {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Log enough to reconstruct a run from its logs:\n"
msgstr "Journalise assez pour reconstituer une exécution à partir de ses logs :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**At the start, log what the run received.** Log the backend name, the number of circuits, and the other settings that change between runs.\n"
msgstr "**Au début, journalise ce que l'exécution a reçu.** Journalise le nom du backend, le nombre de circuits et les autres paramètres qui changent d'une exécution à l'autre.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log the start and end of each stage.** Use fixed messages that you can search for.\n"
msgstr "**Journalise le début et la fin de chaque étape.** Utilise des messages fixes que tu peux rechercher.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log iterations at a fixed interval.** For example, log a line such as `iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` every 10 iterations, instead of every iteration.\n"
msgstr "**Journalise les itérations à intervalle fixe.** Par exemple, journalise une ligne comme `iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` toutes les 10 itérations, plutôt qu'à chaque itération.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log exceptions with `logger.exception()` inside an `except` block.** The line includes the full traceback, even if the workflow recovers from the error.\n"
msgstr "**Journalise les exceptions avec `logger.exception()` dans un bloc `except`.** La ligne inclut la trace d'appels complète, même si le workflow se rétablit après l'erreur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Turn off progress bars.** The logs store each refresh of a progress bar, such as one from `tqdm`, as a separate line. Pass `disable=True` to `tqdm`, or log at an interval instead.\n"
msgstr "**Désactive les barres de progression.** Les logs stockent chaque rafraîchissement d'une barre de progression, comme celle de `tqdm`, sous forme de ligne séparée. Passe `disable=True` à `tqdm`, ou journalise plutôt à intervalle régulier.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Keep the logs small.** Do not log large data, such as every shot. A managed workflow keeps only the newest 50 MB of logs for each job.\n"
msgstr "**Garde les logs petits.** Ne journalise pas de grandes quantités de données, comme chaque shot. Un workflow géré ne conserve que les 50 Mo de logs les plus récents pour chaque job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Use the words \"error\" and \"exception\" only in messages about failures.** If a failed job did not [report its error](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that include these words.\n"
msgstr "**Utilise les mots « error » et « exception » uniquement dans les messages concernant des échecs.** Si un job en échec n'a pas [signalé son erreur](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), l'exception que `job.result()` lève ne contient que les lignes de log qui comprennent ces mots.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: report errors with send_error() {#best-practice-report-errors-with-send-error}"
msgstr "Bonne pratique : signaler les erreurs avec send_error() {#best-practice-report-errors-with-send-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status, and the traceback goes to the logs. A managed workflow does not store the error, even for a `ServerlessError`. `job.error_message()` returns `{}`, and the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that include `error` or `exception`. Checks of argument types and ranges belong in an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), which rejects a bad run before the job starts.\n"
msgstr "Lorsque le workflow lève une exception, le job se termine avec le statut `ERROR`, et la trace d'appels va dans les logs. Un workflow géré ne stocke pas l'erreur, même pour une `ServerlessError`. `job.error_message()` renvoie `{}`, et l'exception que `job.result()` lève ne contient que les lignes de log qui comprennent `error` ou `exception`. Les vérifications des types et des plages d'arguments relèvent d'un [schéma d'arguments](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), qui rejette une mauvaise exécution avant le démarrage du job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report every error that stops the workflow with `send_error()`, so that your local notebook gets a short error with a code and details:\n"
msgstr "Signale avec `send_error()` chaque erreur qui arrête le workflow, afin que ton notebook local reçoive une erreur courte avec un code et des détails :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException` with the same text.\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` lève une `QiskitServerlessException` avec le même texte.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, raise `ServerlessError` where the error happens, and wrap the code of your entrypoint in a `try` block that sends any error with `send_error()`. A workflow adds this handler to Catalog Functions, but not to managed workflows:\n"
msgstr "Pour activer cela, lève `ServerlessError` à l'endroit où l'erreur se produit, et entoure le code de ton point d'entrée d'un bloc `try` qui envoie toute erreur avec `send_error()`. Un workflow ajoute ce gestionnaire aux Catalog Functions, mais pas aux workflows gérés :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Raise the error again.** The final `raise` keeps the traceback in the logs and ends the job with the `ERROR` status.\n"
msgstr "**Relève l'erreur.** Le `raise` final conserve la trace d'appels (traceback) dans les logs et termine le job avec le statut `ERROR`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Subclass `ServerlessError` to name a group of errors.** The handler sends the name of the class, such as `InputError`, as the `exception` field.\n"
msgstr "**Crée une sous-classe de `ServerlessError` pour nommer un groupe d'erreurs.** Le gestionnaire envoie le nom de la classe, par exemple `InputError`, dans le champ `exception`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other exceptions also reach the handler.** They get the code `1`, and their `repr()` becomes the message, such as `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"
msgstr "**Les autres exceptions atteignent aussi le gestionnaire.** Elles reçoivent le code `1`, et leur `repr()` devient le message, par exemple `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: custom (user) workflows run their entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py (fleets_runner.py _upload_custom_image_entrypoint). Only provider jobs get the main.tmpl handler, which calls send_error() for an uncaught exception. Should custom jobs get the same handler? Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0: a raised ServerlessError creates no ERROR event, and error_message() returns {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report a problem and continue {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"
msgstr "Signaler un problème et continuer {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`send_error()` does not stop the workflow or change its status, so you can also report problems that the workflow recovers from, such as each circuit that it skips:\n"
msgstr "`send_error()` n'arrête pas le workflow et ne change pas son statut, tu peux donc aussi signaler des problèmes dont le workflow se remet, comme chaque circuit qu'il ignore :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns every error that the workflow reported, including the errors of a job that ended with the `DONE` status. See [Find the cause of an error](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-error).\n"
msgstr "`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` renvoie toutes les erreurs que le workflow a signalées, y compris les erreurs d'un job qui s'est terminé avec le statut `DONE`. Consulte [Trouver la cause d'une erreur](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-error).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pass numbers and strings in `args`.** `error_message()` shows only the first item of a list.\n"
msgstr "**Passe des nombres et des chaînes dans `args`.** `error_message()` n'affiche que le premier élément d'une liste.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Check the return value.** If a workflow cannot store the error, for example because the code runs outside a job, `send_error()` writes the error to the logs and returns `False`.\n"
msgstr "**Vérifie la valeur de retour.** Si un workflow ne peut pas stocker l'erreur, par exemple parce que le code s'exécute en dehors d'un job, `send_error()` écrit l'erreur dans les logs et renvoie `False`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm which error codes user workflows should use. Catalog Function codes come from the IBM Quantum error code registry, which might not apply to user workflows. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clean up when a job is canceled {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"
msgstr "Nettoyer lorsqu'un job est annulé {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint, uploads the final logs, and shuts down the environment. Without a handler, Python stops immediately, and `finally` blocks do not run. The workflow also tries to cancel the QPU jobs and sessions that the workflow started with `get_runtime_service()`. See [Cancel linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Lorsque tu annules un job, le workflow envoie `SIGTERM` à ton point d'entrée, téléverse les logs finaux et arrête l'environnement. Sans gestionnaire, Python s'arrête immédiatement et les blocs `finally` ne s'exécutent pas. Le workflow essaie aussi d'annuler les jobs QPU et les sessions qu'il a démarrés avec `get_runtime_service()`. Consulte [Annuler les jobs QPU liés](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep partial work, register a handler for `SIGTERM`. Your local notebook then gets the partial result from a canceled job:\n"
msgstr "Pour conserver le travail partiel, enregistre un gestionnaire pour `SIGTERM`. Ton notebook local obtient alors le résultat partiel d'un job annulé :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, add the handler at the start of your entrypoint:\n"
msgstr "Pour activer cela, ajoute le gestionnaire au début de ton point d'entrée :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`sys.exit()` in the handler raises `SystemExit` in the code that is running, so `finally` blocks run before the script ends. The job still ends with the `CANCELED` status.\n"
msgstr "`sys.exit()` dans le gestionnaire lève `SystemExit` dans le code en cours d'exécution, donc les blocs `finally` s'exécutent avant la fin du script. Le job se termine quand même avec le statut `CANCELED`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the handler short, because the workflow shuts down the environment soon after `SIGTERM`. For long runs, also save checkpoints, so that a later run can resume after a job fails or reaches the 24-hour limit. See [Best practice: checkpoint long jobs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Garde le gestionnaire court, car le workflow arrête l'environnement peu après `SIGTERM`. Pour les longues exécutions, enregistre aussi des points de contrôle, afin qu'une exécution ultérieure puisse reprendre après l'échec d'un job ou l'atteinte de la limite de 24 heures. Consulte [Bonne pratique : placer des points de contrôle dans les longs jobs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm the time between SIGTERM and shutdown. The cancel is a Code Engine hard stop (fleets/handler.py cancel_job, cancel_processing_tasks=True), and the repo sets no grace period. Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0, the real fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py, and docker stop: the handler runs, save_result() writes the result, and result() on a CANCELED job returns it (the result endpoint does not check the status). Confirm on Fleets that a result written in the handler reaches storage before the hard stop. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Prochaines étapes {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to start a job and read its status, logs, and result.\n"
"- [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) to save checkpoints that a later run can resume from.\n"
"- [Choose a compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) to run your workflow with more CPU, memory, or GPU resources.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommandations\">\n"
"- [Exécute un workflow géré](/guides/run-managed-workflow) pour démarrer un job et lire son statut, ses logs et son résultat.\n"
"- [Gère les fichiers entre les exécutions](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) pour enregistrer des points de contrôle à partir desquels une exécution ultérieure peut reprendre.\n"
"- [Choisis un profil de calcul](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) pour exécuter ton workflow avec plus de ressources CPU, de mémoire ou de GPU.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
